goldenland-realestate-v2 (project) — AI Assist workflow + architecture/test quirks:
• Workflow (USER PREFERENCE — missing it gets called out): per implement-skill ticket, load the originating issue via gh and read the 'Parent' section + acceptance criteria. Two-axis code review (standards + spec) via parallel sub-agents is mandatory before commit; write the review ledger to docs/agents/reviews/<issue-number>.md. Never skip the Resolve step: `gh issue close` with summary (commit SHA, test results, ledger path), appending pointer to #1's 'Implementation Decisions'.
• Architecture: shared ContentSuggestionValidator base for Property/Complex — fixed field set, plain-text title/meta (rejects entity-encoded markup), 60/160/3000 limits, restricted safe-HTML descriptions; Complex never carries sub_description even on failure. Bilingual (#8): English synthesized first; Burmese lane adds my_accepted_at/my_error; Property title/content translate, Complex description/meta translate, title stays English-only. ContentTranslationAgent + OpenRouter impl; needs 'Translate:ContentSuggestion' permission.
• Image observations (#9/#10): keyed by media_id (Spatie row = version); ensure() reuses stored non-failed observations; strict usable/description/error shape; generators send observation summaries as text, not raw images; CheckboxList in shared ManagesContentSuggestions trait; logos never count as evidence; deterministic agents ignore observations.
• Web search (#11): SearchAnchor value object (privacy-safe phrase + official domain; never call getTranslation on it — Complex title non-translatable would throw); WebSearchAgent + OpenRouter impl (web_search tool, citations); WebEvidenceService; web_evidence JSON on suggestions; defaults deduped onto AiConfiguration constants.
• Test fakes bundle at provider boundaries: propertyProviderFake()/complexProviderFake() include imageObservationFake(); install webSearchFake() in every test setup where generate() runs, or the real agent runs and errors.
• Test quirks: call aiAssistAdminUser() exactly once per test (second call adds another Gate::before denying other users); Spatie caches getMedia per instance — use a fresh model after media deletion; fillForm/mergeState merges list state element-wise — checkbox arrays need a direct set(); assert notification bodies via Notification instance assertions; review-modal evidence lives in component state, not in modal HTML — assert on state. <!-- created=2026-08-08, last=2026-08-08 -->
